course: dictionary
lesson: 10083
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. The word «theory» is a good example. «I have a theory about who ate the cake» means an idea someone has, which may or may not be true. But in science, a theory is a well-tested explanation that is supported by a lot of evidence.
explain: Look at the words around it. If the sentence is about science, nature or evidence, the meaning is the strong science one. If the sentence sounds like a detective or a friend guessing, it means an idea that may or may not be true. Ask yourself: is this a guess, or a well-tested explanation?
explain: «In theory» is a phrase with its own meaning. «A chihuahua and a Great Dane could in theory have puppies together» means it should be possible if things go as planned, even though it is unlikely in real life. Read the whole phrase, not just the single word, to catch what it means.
fact: A theory can mean a well-tested explanation of how nature works, such as the theory of gravity.
fact: A theory can also mean an idea someone has, which may or may not be true, such as «I have a theory about who ate the cake».
fact: «In theory» means what should happen if things go as planned, though it might not.
fact: Theory can also mean the ideas and rules of a subject, as opposed to practice, like music theory.
fact: A conspiracy theory is a false story about a secret plan.
exercise: «In science a theory is a big explanation backed by a mountain of evidence.» What does theory mean in this sentence? | A rule for playing music | *A well-tested explanation supported by lots of evidence | A type of cake | A wild guess with no evidence at all
exercise: Sam says, «I have a theory about who ate the cake.» What does theory mean here? | A plan that always works | Music notes and scales | A proven law of nature | *An idea that may or may not be true
exercise: «A chihuahua and a Great Dane could in theory have puppies together.» What does in theory mean? | *It should be possible if things go as planned, though it might not happen | It is a sad story | It is impossible and could never be | It is definitely happening right now
test: In «Mia is studying music theory», what does theory mean? | A loud noise from a speaker | *The ideas and rules of music, like notes and scales | A guess about who wrote a song | A proven law of nature
test: «A conspiracy theory is a false story about a secret plan.» What is a conspiracy theory? | A true story about a lost city | A rule for playing an instrument | *A false story about a secret plan | A proven explanation of how nature works
exam: Which sentence uses theory in the science sense? | Her theory about the cake turned out to be wrong | In theory, we could fly to the moon tomorrow | *The theory of gravity has been tested many times | I have a theory about the lost key
